# D-229, symptom one: supersession matched across lineages.
#
# `LINKS_ARCHIVABLE` asked for "a later assertion for the same interval key"
# without asking whose, so a branch asserting at an ancestor's key made the
# ancestor's own open, current row look superseded — and one ordinary `archive`
# then took it. Measured at 0.14.12: the trunk stops reaching `b`.
#
# The clause that fixes it is `newer.branch_id = links.branch_id` in
# `src/temporal/archive.rs`. Remove it and this case fails; that is the
# mutation D-268 records.
fork parent=main child=x
assert key=0 branch=x closed=0
archive
